\noindent \emph{Note}: If a reference has multiple authors, the names are printed separated by commas, and the authorship information is put in brackets, using the name 'et al.' if there are more than two authors. If a reference has three or more authors, all the authors' names are printed the first time the reference is cited in the text, and the subsequent citation refers to the work as 'Ibid.'

